{"id": "EUVD-2026-97648", "enisaUuid": "0946ea0b-52ce-3173-9ff9-c581db2e0133", "description": "better-auth from 1.3.8-beta.3 before 1.7.0-rc.3 contains a UI misrepresentation vulnerability in the deviceAuthorization plugin because GET /device omits the requesting client_id and scope. Attackers can start a device request via /device/code, trick signed-in users into approving the code, then redeem it at /device/token for a live session token.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-12T16:05:30", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/security/advisories/GHSA-q84f-53jg-9ppm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/better-auth-1.3.8-beta.3-before-1.7.0-rc.3-device-authorization-phishing-via-device"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v9c8-wq66-wf8g", "CVE-2026-109346"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ccc329cf-d9b7-33bb-97f1-da7ca216c6af", "product": {"name": "better-auth", "vendor": {"name": "better-auth"}}, "product_version": "1.3.8-beta.3 <1.7.0-rc.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8c5961e0-7611-3935-8dd2-a9f0cc3bee7d", "vendor": {"name": "better-auth"}}], "isExploited": false}